  "articleBody": "Being accused of domestic violence can be a really frightening experience, and it's easy to feel like your world is turning upside down. The first thing you need to do is understand the seriousness of the situation. These charges carry significant legal and personal consequences, impacting your freedom, reputation, and relationships. It’s absolutely critical to avoid making any statements to law enforcement without a lawyer present. Anything you say can and will be used against you, even if you believe you’re just explaining your side. Immediately seeking legal counsel from an experienced domestic violence defense lawyer is paramount. They can advise you on your rights, help you navigate the complex legal system, and begin building a strong defense. This might involve gathering evidence, interviewing witnesses, and challenging the prosecution's case. Ignoring the charges or trying to handle them alone is one of the biggest mistakes you can make. Your future depends on a swift and informed response.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-26"
